# tally 2.2.1 (#236, 236.1), L §4.3 and §5.14: a window `at` "evaluates the instance once per law-date class";
# "otherwise §4.4's rule holds". shut's key's where is true in the first law-date class (2026-03-10 .. 03-14) and false in the second
# (day2 governs from 2026-03-15), so whether shut[p] exists is the window's hole, naming win_day, and no later version
# answers it (the where is read at the ask's cut K, E §4.1 step 1); the refusal of spare's end holding 100.00 PLN is
# one only the days it doesn't exist give, so it doesn't outrank that hole. tally 2.2 answered the hole by the version
# known 2026-01-02 and booked shut: 0.00 PLN (the M3 gate's win/w1_differs_nowait.tally).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "p"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind rents: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place spare: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..2026-06-30

place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input rent_amt: money PLN

input back_amt: money PLN

input act_day: date

input back_day: date

input zero: int

input one_amt: money PLN

input gap_day: date

input d_open: date

input win_day: date

move rent[m in months]: rents
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

move shut[p in accounts on d_open where act_day < back_day]: transfers
  on d_open
  at win_day
  leg cash from p to landlord amount back_amt

version v
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 900.00 PLN
  back_amt = 100.00 PLN

version v2
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-15
  replace rent_amt = 950.00 PLN "raise"

version day
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  act_day = 2026-04-05
  back_day = 2026-04-20

version day2
  cite plan
  governs 2026-03-15..
  known 2026-01-02
  replace act_day = 2026-04-25

version fixed
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  zero = 0
  one_amt = 1.00 PLN
  d_open = 2026-01-01
  win_day = window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-20)
  opening[spare] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "w"

ask q: bal(spare, 2026-06-30) law cut
=== expect
q: ?"date within window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-20) not precise enough for the law date of shut" (shut)
  unknown day: win_day
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
warning: WARN-UNREAD input gap_day is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input one_amt is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input zero is read by nothing
